# Generated pages.
#
# Netlify runs `python3 build.py` on every deploy and the release gate decides
# what exists on the day it runs. Committing the output would freeze a
# date-gated site at whatever date it was last built on, and the repository
# would disagree with the site every morning.
#
# Anchored to the root on purpose: /pathivu/ is generated HTML, while
# assets/img/pathivu/ is the photographs and is committed.
/*.html
/en/
/kathai/
/pathivu/
/sitemap.xml
/robots.txt
/niladhamma.ics

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# macOS
.DS_Store

# One-off exports. Committing these would publish them at the site root; if a
# PDF should be downloadable, generate it into assets/ and link to it instead.
/dana-*.pdf

# Reports: the generator and the photographs are source; the rendered
# document is not, for the same reason the site's pages are not.
/reports/*.html
/reports/*.pdf
